{"id": "DcWLTTOvf8M", "title": "Video by nick_saraev", "description": "Comment \"DEEPSEEK\" to get DeepSeek Harness and build your own custom AI agent.\n\nDeepSeek just launched their own free version of Claude Code.\n\nIt has already crossed 180k stars on GitHub in under a week.\n\nIt's called DeepSeek Harness.\n\nUnlike Claude Code, it's fully customizable.\n\nIt's built on the idea that everything inside it is a plugin.\n\nIncluding the model, the tools, the memory, and even the agent loop itself.\n\nSo you just swap out whatever piece you want.\n\nYou can build your own custom AI agent from scratch, piece by piece, exactly how you imagine it.\n\nWhich means you can run it with any AI model locally, without depending on one single provider.\n\nYou can even call Claude Code and Codex as sub agents inside it, letting different tools handle different parts of the job.\n\nPlus it comes with 53 tools right out of the box, so you're not starting from an empty setup.\n\nAnd it's completely free and open source.\n\nThink of it like Lego blocks for AI agents, every single piece is swappable, removable, and replaceable.\n\nMost tools lock you into their own model and their own logic, no matter what you actually need.\n\nThis one hands you the entire architecture and lets you rebuild it however you want, from the ground up.\n\n#deepseek #deepseekharness #claudecode #aiagent #opensourceai", "channel": "nick_saraev", "uploader_id": "72269881052", "uploader": "Nick Saraev", "timestamp": 1787410751, "like_count": 6282, "comment_count": 4452, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1588426649428091a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 66.149, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.famd5-5.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQML7rxQU3EuQfiraYNykM2i0Yujb4KtG6PCNC8F5WM8goC8K6KpTT1xdd15nnbP_jawhoFtrhLl-1nCZzKVXjuVoV9OpGaJBuDacJs.mp4?_nc_cat=104&_nc_oc=AdoC3